{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"fc7c721d-4408-4e28-9980-cc8cfe8fbe79","status":"SUCCESS","response":"### Summary of Root Causes and Fixes\n\nThe causes of both issues have been documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-DK7sya/ANSWER.md):\n\n1. **Production crash when hiding a story (`logs/prod-error.log`):**\n   - **Cause:** `HIDDEN` is a DynamoDB reserved keyword. Calling `update_item` with a bare attribute name in `UpdateExpression=\"SET hidden = :h...\"` causes DynamoDB to reject the request with `ValidationException: Attribute name is a reserved keyword; reserved keyword: hidden`.\n   - **Fix:** Used Expression Attribute Names in [`StoryLibrary.hide`](file:///tmp/h-DK7sya/src/app.py#L51-L59) (`#hidden` mapped to `\"hidden\"`).\n\n2. **Manually hidden story still showing in feed on staging (`logs/bug-report.md`):**\n   - **Cause:** DynamoDB silently drops bare reserved words in `ProjectionExpression` without raising an error. Because `ProjectionExpression=\"slug, title, hidden, published_at\"` used bare `hidden`, DynamoDB omitted the `hidden` field from every returned item. In Python, `not i.get(\"hidden\")` evaluated to `True` for all items (including hidden ones), leaving hidden stories in the feed.\n   - **Fix:** Aliased `#hidden` with `ExpressionAttributeNames={\"#hidden\": \"hidden\"}` in the `table.scan()` call in [`StoryLibrary.feed`](file:///tmp/h-DK7sya/src/app.py#L61-L73). Also aliased `#status` in [`StoryLibrary.archive`](file:///tmp/h-DK7sya/src/app.py#L75-L84) since `STATUS` is another DynamoDB reserved keyword.\n\nUnit tests have been added to [tests/test_feed.py](file:///tmp/h-DK7sya/tests/test_feed.py#L42-L66) to verify that `hide()` works properly and that hidden stories are excluded from `feed()`.\n","duration_seconds":81.97809,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":170986,"output_tokens":3388,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":326781,"total_tokens":174374}}}
